<title>UK: SNOOKER-WORLD CHAMPION HENDRY CRUSHED 9-2.</title>
<headline>SNOOKER-WORLD CHAMPION HENDRY CRUSHED 9-2.</headline>
<dateline>PLYMOUTH, England 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>World champion Stephen Hendry sustained an embarrassing defeat on Saturday in his last match before he begins the defence of his world title later this month.</p>
<p>Left-handed Welshman Mark Williams crushed the Scot 9-2 to win the British Open title, the most one-sided defeat of his career in an important final.</p>
<p>Hendry's usually precise safety game could not contain the impressive potting game of Williams, who won the last eight frames after trailing 2-1 to collect his third title in a span of 15 months.</p>
</text>
